  "query_preview": "/Monday through Thursday/...\nBy early next week next week the high pressure will be well over \nNE CONUS and the open wave trough will begin to be absorbed into \nthe mean SW flow head of the next incoming low pressure system \ndiving down the western coastline. Another low chance (20-30%) of \nshowers manifest Monday morning across the higher terrain, however\nyet again, if anything does develop total accumulations are \nexpected to be near zero. By Tuesday, deep troughing and strong \nnegative height anomalies will amplify and intensify along the \nwest coast, however confidence in the timing and depth of this \nfeature remains low to moderate. The ECMWF deterministic is \nforecasting a slower and more robust rainfall scenario, while the \nGFS deterministic provides a faster and more mild rainfall \npotential. Regardless, the timing of any rainfall potential is \nhighlighting Wednesday and Thursday. Additionally, with the \nuncertainty of this next system a wide spread in NBM temperatures \nhave presented themselves throughout the week, though below normal\nhighs are likely.",
